herefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{3}^{2y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={3}^{x}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{3}^{-2y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={3}^{x}"] ["math" "{3}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={3}^{-2y}"] ["math" "{3}^{2y-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "{3}^{2y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={3}^{x}"] ["math" "{3}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={3}^{-2y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{3}^{2y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={3}^{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/qu