hen it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x"] ["math" "\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1"] ["math" "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}"] ["math" "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-157692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-157692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{y}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x},\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n{e}^{-y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-157692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-157692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-157692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-y}"] ["math" "{e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{y}"] ["math" "{e}^{-y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}"] ["math" "{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{y}"] ["math" "{e}^{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-157692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{x}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{x}+C\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-14246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{\\sqrt{x}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\sqrt{x}}+C"] ["math" "y={e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "{e}^{y}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={e}^{x}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & ={x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\text{ }y={x}^{3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y}$ for $x\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡y=\\frac{1}{x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "4{e}^{y}={x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y}=2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2y}=x+C"] ["math" "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-154359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x{e}^{-y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{2}+C"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-3850" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}+1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y) & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y)=x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+y+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+C)"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+1)+C"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\cdot 3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\int {y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{1/3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=(6x+C)^{3}"] ["math" "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{6x+C}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}"] ["math" "y={x}^{6}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-51256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-158015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}"] ["math" "y={e}^{{x}^{2}/2}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-158015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=0$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}"] ["math" "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] ["math" "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K"] ["math" "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8305" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y}=2x\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}+x+C\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=({x}^{2}+x)^{2}"] ["math" "y=({x}^{2}+x+C)^{2}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x}{2})}^{2}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}+x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2}=2{x}^{1/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & =3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2})}^{2/3} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{3C}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-8304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=3{x}^{1/2}+K"] ["math" "y=3{x}^{1/3}+K"] ["math" "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}"] ["math" "y={({x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}"] ["math" "y={({x}^{2/3}+K)}^{1/2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-8304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-79660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $(xy)^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ for $x\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-79660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(xy)^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}=C-\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3} & =C-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =3C-\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{3C-\\frac{3}{x}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=3C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-79660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-79660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-79660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{1}{x}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{K}{x}+1}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{K+\\frac{1}{x}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{K-\\frac{2}{x}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-79660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(1+2x) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =x+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{y}={x}^{2}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ec922797d4c37acbca1781ba045d6de34dbdb3272845aa74b441f66eabb810e"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{2x+C}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}"] ["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x}+C"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+x}+C"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+C}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "q-14253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+C}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b1bb180c9e0f11f93a27710394182cee8fcb15c7d46cbc3580f1e9fc2f1691b"} {"question" "e-10849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $x,y \\geq 0,$ separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2xy}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10849.json" "file_sha256" "bcf520050a87378e04d859edcc8db85e258dbbb1d43df8cfefe7f330c4526897"} {"question" "e-10849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{g(y)} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} =  \\sqrt{2x} \\cdot  \\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{y}} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\sqrt{2x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10849.json" "file_sha256" "bcf520050a87378e04d859edcc8db85e258dbbb1d43df8cfefe7f330c4526897"} {"question" "e-10997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    \\dfrac{x}{y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10997.json" "file_sha256" "b335c0fe38f222588aaae2888d5bfa22c4e7108ae113efc3af2f71261a999dec"} {"question" "e-10997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10997.json" "file_sha256" "b335c0fe38f222588aaae2888d5bfa22c4e7108ae113efc3af2f71261a999dec"} {"question" "e-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' = \\dfrac {x^2}{y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10832.json" "file_sha256" "f8fd12f51042371f834f9bbde315713093900153e983b9e60fc2eecb7d5f8998"} {"question" "e-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + C.\n$$\n\nWe can express the solution in the form $y = y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = 2C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10832.json" "file_sha256" "f8fd12f51042371f834f9bbde315713093900153e983b9e60fc2eecb7d5f8998"} {"question" "e-10833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' + 2xy = 0$ for $y\\neq 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10833.json" "file_sha256" "9e82b8f67fa194f48a1e8775f5847c138bb592feb33120741147b5c836ba16a4"} {"question" "e-10833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln \\vert y \\vert = -x^2 + C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y = y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = e^C$  and $K > 0.$ \n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ke^{-x^2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036385/example-10833.json" "file_sha256" "9e82b8f67fa194f48a1e8775f5847c138bb592feb33120741147b5c836ba16a4"}] "usage" {"q-14253" [] "q-14257" [] "e-10833" [] "q-8305" [] "e-10997" [] "q-158014" [] "q-3850" [] "q-158117" [] "q-157692" [] "e-10849" [] "q-158026" [] "q-158035" [] "e-10832" [] "q-8303" [] "q-154359" []} "basis" 1243 "retractions" [[17592186069009 :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation:\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{x + y}$"] [17592186069009 :question/worked-solution "Use $e^{x+y}=e^xe^y$ and multiply both sides by $e^{-y}$:\n$$e^{-y}\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^x.$$\nThe left-hand factor depends only on $y$, and the right-hand side depends only on $x$."] [17592186069003 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{2x}{e^{y}}$."] [17592186069003 :question/worked-solution "Multiply by $e^y$ and integrate:\n$$e^y\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x,\\qquad \\int e^y\\,dy=\\int2x\\,dx.$$\nThus $e^y=x^2+C$. Equivalently, $y=\\ln(x^2+C)$ on an interval where $x^2+C>0$."] [17592186069003 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186068987 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y^{\\prime } = y^{2} + 1$."] [17592186068987 :question/worked-solution "Separate the variables and integrate:\n$$\\frac{dy}{1+y^2}=dx,\\qquad \\arctan y=x+C.$$\nThus $y=\\tan(x+C)$ on any interval between consecutive poles. Differentiating gives $y'=\\sec^2(x+C)=1+y^2$."] [17592186068987 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186069460 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} - (\\cos x)y = 0$ for $y \\ne 0$."] [17592186069460 :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the equation as $y'=y\\cos x$. For $y\\ne0$,\n$$\\frac{dy}{y}=\\cos x\\,dx,\\qquad \\ln|y|=\\sin x+C.$$\nTherefore $y=Ke^{\\sin x}$, where $K\\ne0$."] [17592186069460 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186069459 :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y^{\\prime } - \\sqrt{y} = 2x\\sqrt{y}$ for $y \\ne 0$."] [17592186069459 :question/worked-solution "Rearrange to $y'=(2x+1)\\sqrt y$. Since the real-valued problem assumes $y\\ne0$, we have $y>0$, so\n$$\\frac{dy}{\\sqrt y}=(2x+1)\\,dx,\\qquad 2\\sqrt y=x^2+x+C.$$\nThus\n$$y=\\left(\\frac{x^2+x+C}{2}\\right)^2.$$\nUse this formula only on intervals where $x^2+x+C>0$, as required by the unsquared equation."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186065717 17592186065718 17592186065719 17592186065720 17592186065721 17592186065813 17592186065814 17592186065815 17592186065816 17592186065817 17592186065849 17592186065850 17592186065851 17592186065852 17592186065853 17592186068286 17592186068287 17592186068288 17592186068289 17592186068290 17592186068292 17592186068293 17592186068294 17592186068295 17592186068296 17592186290008 17592186290009 17592186290010 17592186290011 17592186290012 17592186290050 17592186290051 17592186290052 17592186290053 17592186290054 17592186290078 17592186290079 17592186290080 17592186290081 17592186290082 17592186290092 17592186290093 17592186290094 17592186290095 17592186290096 17592186290099 17592186290100 17592186290101 17592186290102 17592186290103 17592186290106 17592186290107 17592186290108 17592186290109 17592186290110] "immutable_fields" [[17592186065716 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065716 :answer-field/id] [17592186065716 :answer-field/key] [17592186065716 :answer-field/type] [17592186065812 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065812 :answer-field/id] [17592186065812 :answer-field/key] [17592186065812 :answer-field/type] [17592186065848 :answer-field/correct] [17592186065848 :answer-field/id] [17592186065848 :answer-field/key] [17592186065848 :answer-field/type] [17592186068285 :answer-field/correct] [17592186068285 :answer-field/id] [17592186068285 :answer-field/key] [17592186068285 :answer-field/type] [17592186068291 :answer-field/correct] [17592186068291 :answer-field/id] [17592186068291 :answer-field/key] [17592186068291 :answer-field/type] [17592186290007 :answer-field/correct] [17592186290007 :answer-field/id] [17592186290007 :answer-field/key] [17592186290007 :answer-field/type] [17592186290049 :answer-field/correct] [17592186290049 :answer-field/id] [17592186290049 :answer-field/key]